    <description>ALF-RS-04 FR10: fires when AF_ApprovalStatus__c changes to Approved. Hands the trade-in back to the initiating rep (Owner = AF_InitiatingSalesRep__c, out of the AF_Q_UsedCarTeam queue) and notifies them via email + Custom Notification to record the outcome and continue the deal. Real gap found and fixed 2026-09-08 during ALF-RS-04 full-persona-cycle testing: the email step originally used the emailAlert core action (Appraisal.AF_EA_Appraisal_ApprovalApproved, a Workflow EmailAlert) - deployed clean, the flow completed with no fault (confirmed via the Owner reassignment succeeding), but a debug-log capture of a real live approval showed ZERO EMAIL_QUEUE entries and zero resulting EmailMessage records. The one EmailMessage this org previously showed for a similar-looking case (&quot;Approval Needed: Quote Discount...&quot;) turned out NOT to come from an emailAlert action at all - grepped the whole source tree and confirmed AF_EA_Quote_DiscountApproved (the Workflow alert with the same shape) is not referenced by any deployed Flow or ApprovalProcess, so that prior EmailMessage came from a different mechanism entirely, not proof the emailAlert pattern works here. Switched to emailSimple (logEmailOnSend=true) instead, the one pattern proven repeatedly this session (AF_FL_Appraisal_EvaluationSubmit, AF_FL_AppraisalItem_EvaluationComplete originally, etc.) to reliably create a real, queryable EmailMessage in this org. Updated 2026-09-09: user asked for the customer Contact to also receive this confirmation, not just the rep. Added Get_Contact (via AF_Contact__c) and Formula_RecipientEmails, which sends to both rep and Contact (comma-separated emailAddresses) when the Contact has an email, falling back to rep-only otherwise - same shared email body for both audiences per user&apos;s explicit choice.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;margin:0;padding:16px;background-color:#F4F4F6;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #E2E5EA;border-top:4px solid #0B2545;padding:20px 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;color:#0B2545;&quot;&gt;Trade-In Approved&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;The trade-in valuation for &lt;strong&gt;&apos; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber} &amp; &apos;&lt;/strong&gt; was approved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;Record the customer outcome and continue with the quotation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&apos;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Approved: Trade-In &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_RecipientEmails</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    ISBLANK({!Get_Contact.Email}),
    {!Get_Rep_ForEmail.Email},
    {!Get_Rep_ForEmail.Email} &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; {!Get_Contact.Email}
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;The trade-in valuation for &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber} &amp; &quot; was approved. Record the customer outcome and continue with the quotation.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifTitle</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Trade-In Approved: &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalNumber}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Appraisal Approval Approved {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Appraisal Approval Approved</label>
